Package: mremoteng
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/KeithMarex/mremoteng-linux
Depends: openssh-client, libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1 (>= 3.0), libstdc++6 (>= 6), libfontconfig1 (>= 2.12.6), libicu76 | libicu74 | libicu72, libssl3t64 | libssl3, libx11-6, libxcursor1, libxext6, libxfixes3, libxi6, libxrandr2, libice6, libsm6
Recommends: inetutils-telnet | telnet, xdg-utils
Suggests: rsh-redone-client
Description: remote connections manager (community Linux port of mRemoteNG)
 mRemoteNG for Linux keeps remote connections in a tree and opens them in
 tabs: SSH, Telnet, rlogin, raw TCP, PowerShell and local terminal sessions,
 and SFTP and FTP/FTPS file transfers. Web addresses open in the browser and
 AnyDesk connections in the AnyDesk client.
 .
 Its connection files (confCons.xml) are those of mRemoteNG for Windows, so
 a team can share one file, including its encrypted passwords. SSH uses
 OpenSSH, so ssh_config, keys, the agent and known_hosts apply.
 .
 This is a community port; it is not made by the mRemoteNG project.
